OL,1,V7w3s7s35E                         G7/22
OL,2,V55555555CIRAQ DISMISSES
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CMOVES TO SAVE BAZOFT
OL,4,         C
OL,5, Iraq has dismissed efforts to save the
OL,6, life of Observer reporter Farzad Bazoft
OL,7, and insisted he had a fair trial.
OL,9, Information Minister Latif Nussif
OL,10, Jassem said in Baghdad attempts to save
OL,11, Mr Bazoft "constitute blatant inter-
OL,12, ference in our internal affairs".
OL,14, Mr Jassem described the international
OL,15, outcry over the case as a "fabricated
OL,16, clamour" and said he was tried fairly.
OL,18, Meanwhile, the daughter of British
OL,19, nurse Daphne Parish, jailed for 15
OL,20, years for helping Mr Bazoft, has seen
OL,21, the Iraqi ambassador in London.
OL,23,F]DFrom 12-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
