OL,1,V7w3s7s35B                        G10/22
OL,2,V55555555CGORBACHEV'S 'ALARM'
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5COVER LITHUANIA
OL,5, President Gorbachev has said he is
OL,6, "alarmed" by Lithuania's declaration
OL,7, of independence from the Soviet Union.
OL,9, He told the Soviet parliament that the
OL,10, decision affected the interests of the
OL,11, whole of the USSR.
OL,13, He said the Kremlin would begin studies
OL,14, of the Lithuanian decision whiah could
OL,15, soon be matched by the other two Baltia
OL,16, republics, Latvia and Estonia.
OL,18, Baltic delegates to the Congress of
OL,19, People's Deputies had planned to
OL,20, boycott the meeting but changed their
OL,21, strategy to argue their case.
OL,23,F]DFrom 12-03-90 / teletextarchive.com
